{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Archimedean.InvariantFormTransport","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Archimedean.InvariantFormTransport","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Matrix.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Real.Basic"],"declarations":2,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.InvariantFormTransport.sq_pos_of_gauge","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.InvariantFormTransport.sq_pos_of_gauge","kind":"theorem","line":53,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/InvariantFormTransport.lean#L53-L60","doc":"**The sign of the Schur scale is gauge-invariant (over `ℝ`).** Every\nadmissible real intertwiner gauge `μ ≠ 0` rescales the pulled-back Gram by\n`μ² > 0` — so whether the τ-image of the Markov Gram is a *positive* multiple\nof the Hodge Gram is a frame-independent question: the honest frame-free\nconsistency test of the τ-identification (positivity of the Markov Gram at\n`q₀` + positivity of the Hodge form ⟹ the identification requires `c > 0`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.InvariantFormTransport.invariantForm_pullback_smul","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.InvariantFormTransport.invariantForm_pullback_smul","kind":"theorem","line":43,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/InvariantFormTransport.lean#L43-L51","doc":"**Gauge covariance of the pulled-back form.** Rescaling the intertwiner\n`P ↦ μ • P` (the Schur gauge freedom) rescales the pulled-back form\n`Pᵀ * M * P` by `μ²`. Hence the proportionality scale `c` of\n`TauS5EquivarianceReduction.tauImage_proportional_hodge` is well-defined only\nmodulo squares of the intertwiner gauge. ","signatureChunk":0}]}